[Buzzer]

29
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:34,840
This is really fascinating.

30
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,840
Hi everyone, just here with Tom Servo discussing his art.

31
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,840
So you say Crow gave you the money to do all this, huh?

32
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:46,840
Well, yes. I think he saw in me and my art a kind of truth, you see.

33
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,840
And with his 30 grand plus a matching grant from the Chubb Group of Insurance Companies,

34
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:55,840
I can finally express myself and put down 59,000 on that stable of Trotters down south.

35
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,840
Hey, hi Mike.

36
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,840
Servo, I just paid the caterer.

37
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:03,840
It's kind of pricey, but hey, it's the art world, huh?

38
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,840
So, let's take a look at my portraits.

39
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,840
Huh? Hmm, huh?

40
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,840
Hmm, huh?

41
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,840
Wow.

42
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,840
Oh my, wow.

43
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,840
Yeah?

44
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:18,840
Crow is, uh, huh.

45
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,840
Well, you know, Servo, these all...

46
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,840
paint a stark portrait of a cruel despot?

47
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:25,840
Uh, no, I was actually going to say they're all kind of negative.

48
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:29,840
Oh, fine. Why don't you just paint a picture of you in heaven playing golf with clowns?

49
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,840
Now that's not bad. Here, I'll write you a check. Will 30,000 be enough?

50
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,840
I better make it 60. I might want to do an unfiltered.

51
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,840
We'll be right back.

52
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,840
And stab at the canvas.

53
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:49,840
I, uh, thought you were going to paint me playing golf with clowns.

54
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,840
No, no, you want to do yourself tossing kittens into a meek rinder.

55
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,840
I have my notes if you'd like to see them.

56
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,840
Whoa, whoa, hands, prepare to die!

57
00:02:56,840 --> 00:03:00,840
Wait a minute, Jipsy, let's not jump to any conclusions. What's the problem?

58
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:06,840
We're caught in some sort of tractor beam pulling us at a million times the speed of light towards an unknown destination.

59
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:11,840
Time and space are meaningless, and the physical laws are breaking down.

60
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:18,840
All right. See? Oh, wait. We're slowing down. I guess things will be okay.

61
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:24,840
I wonder where we are, though. Of course, I didn't know where we were before, so we might as well be here as anywhere.

62
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,840
That's what I always say.

63
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,840
Hello? Anyone there?

64
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,840
Shoo! Get out of here! Beat it!

65
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:39,840
Please, do not be afraid.

66
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:43,840
Welcome, and try to comprehend us.

67
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,840
Uh, okay.

68
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,840
What's to comprehend?

69
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:53,840
Oh, you are to us as an amoeba is to you, for we are the observers.

70
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,840
And we have evolved beyond language.

71
00:03:56,840 --> 00:04:02,840
We are gratified that you understand our words, for we communicate only with our minds.

72
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,840
Wow!

73
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,840
Except you're talking now.

74
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,840
Yeah!

75
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:11,840
No, no, no, no. Do you see how your comprehension fails you?

76
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:14,840
For we communicate only with our minds.

77
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:20,840
You see, we have evolved beyond the need for bodies, and now we are simply brains.

78
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:24,840
You are as amoebas, but do not be afraid.

79
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,840
No bodies. That is fantastic!

80
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,840
Unbelievable. Well, except you have bodies right now.

81
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,840
Well, yeah, you got a point there, Mike.

82
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,840
Yeah! What the hell?

83
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:39,840
Naturally, we require host bodies for our self-sufficient brains.

84
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:44,840
Wouldn't it be more convenient to just leave your brains in your head?

85
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,840
Right.

86
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:51,840
Convenient? Why, our brains are fully functional for our bodies for up to 50 yards.

87
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:55,840
Well, they may not understand. They are as amoebas.

88
00:04:55,840 --> 00:05:01,840
Look, when you cut it out with this amoeba thing, I am way more evolved than an amoeba palae.

89
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:02,840
Tell you that.

90
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,840
Hush, hush, Croce. Who is that grabbing the towsky there?

91
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,840
She is your friend and another of our guests.

92
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:12,840
We have brought you all here to observe her magnificent experiment.

93
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:16,840
Though we have acquired all knowledge and have evolved infinitely beyond you.

94
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,840
Hi, Mike. Guess I caught you again, huh?

95
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:23,840
Hey, what do you think of these characters? Pretty evolved.

96
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:27,840
She and her companion are our guests.

97
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:30,840
We will use our minds to create anything they need for their comfort.

98
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:36,840
Yeah, pretty nice setup here. Dallas reruns, plenty of long necks. Bobo's happy.

99
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:40,840
Hello, Mike. Oh, this is nice.

100
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:44,840
Sweet deal, even though I am as an amoeba.

101
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,840
Ha! Oh, please. This is beneath my dignity.

102
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:52,840
Anywho, your movie today is something called the thing that couldn't die.

103
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:59,840
Observers, after we're done observing this group, we shall dissect them and display them in our museum.

104
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,840
Other children will be delighted.

105
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:06,840
Do you think the orbiting ones heard?

106
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:13,840
Excellent. Send those who are as an amoeba the movie.

107
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:16,840
Amoeba this. Yeah, get a tan.

108
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,840
Oh, wow!

109
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:31,840
[Buzzer]

110
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:35,840
The weather today, the oceans turn black.

111
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:42,840
The big valley!

112
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:46,840
A strong thermon story.

113
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,840
Couldn't die or wouldn't die.

114
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,840
Plug it in, Joe.

115
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:58,840
Ah! People! They've beamed onto the planet OK Corral.

116
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:02,840
Well, looks like somebody's mama let him grow up to be a cowboy.

117
